In each outer fold, we draw up to 50,000 pairs of held-out molecules and compute the Spearman correlation between their distance and the absolute difference in their activity. A positive value means that molecules further apart differ more in activity. We measure this first in each of the dataset's representations alone, under every distance of Section~\ref{sec:similarity:knn_settings}, with no selection and no importance weighting. We then measure it in the feature spaces of Section~\ref{sec:similarity:spaces}, unweighted and weighted.
