Three limitations apply. QM9 has no result for the best number of features, importance weighting in the four models, or Bayesian optimization. The weighted comparison of distance against activity is missing on five datasets, three of them small-molecule datasets. The comparison with the setting picked again lets the hybrid side choose among more combinations and use importance weighting, so it favors the hybrid.

