Simple choices were often enough. Random forests were the most consistent choice under label noise across the four datasets of Chapter~\ref{chap:robustness}, while the plain and Bayesian neural networks were among the least robust. In the preliminary runs on hERG $K_i$, a hybrid of a few hundred features chosen for the task matched or beat the best single representation used whole, as a model input and for nearest-neighbor prediction (Chapters~\ref{chap:method} and~\ref{chap:similarity}) \textbf{[RESULT NEEDED: full runs]}.

