A new foundation model appears every few months in molecular, protein and antibody modeling. With the hybrid search, a researcher need not choose between their current representation and a new one: they add the new embeddings to the representations searched and re-run the search, which decides whether the new embedding contributes features and, if so, how many and which. A choice often set by familiarity or laboratory convention becomes one measured on each task, repeatable as new representations appear.


